WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.033
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.200
I appreciate
every time you come.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.968
-I've always wanted
to drink water here.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:08.367
You always see, like, the cup

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:09.767
but I don't ever see
anybody drink.

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:11.701
And I always wanted to just have
a little sip of water.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:13.100
-Yeah.
I have to ask you,

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.901
because we talked about this
last time.

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:16.601
You now have a house.
-Yes.

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:18.667
-And last time we talked,
you thought --

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:20.200
you had an ice maker
and you thought

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.968
the Three Stooges
were burglaring your house.

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:24.300
And it made me laugh.
But you have a house.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.167
How is it?
And I heard that Questlove

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:28.701
helped you decide
to move Upstate?

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:30.334
-That's true. He did.

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:32.434
I was looking for a house,
and I was looking

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:34.801
out in some town
that I shouldn't have been in.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.300
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.734
And he was like, "You
need to look where I'm at."

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:40.667
And I looked up there,
and it's quite nice.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:43.400
I do enjoy it.
It's good water.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:46.367
I'm not used to having
neighbors, though.

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:48.934
Like, even still, I've never
seen you before,

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:51.167
like, in the neighborhood.
-i have yet to move in.

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:53.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.601
-So you sent me
to a neighborhood

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:56.300
that you don't even live in?

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:00.434
-I'm not ready yet.
I'm not ready yet.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:02.701
-Yeah, so I'm, like,
the guinea pig

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:05.000
for the neighborhood, now?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.400
-Do you like it?
-It's crazy, though.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.701
Like, when I first got there,

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:12.100
some lady, like,
brought me bread.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.501
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:15.400
She knocked on the door
and was like,

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.334
"I'm your neighbor.
Here's some bread."

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:18.501
-That's so nice.

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:19.934
-Trying to poison me
or something.

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:22.067
-No, Upstate,
that's not what they do.

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:23.734
-If you're watching this, ma'am,

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:25.968
I punted your bread
over two fences.

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:27.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:29.367
-You're too paranoid.
She was being neighborly.

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:31.901
-No, man,
I've lived in apartments

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.434
in New York City my whole life.

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:35.467
I've never met one neighbor.

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:37.534
[ Laughter ]
Not one person.

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:39.834
We don't make eye contact.
We're nice people that way.

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:44.601
Suburbs, I don't trust it.
-I want to ask about Colin Jost,

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.234
your "Weekend Update" co-anchor.

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:48.767
You guys are fantastic together,
by the way.

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.501
Congrats on a great season.
-Oh, stop.

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:52.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:56.667
-He just had a baby.
-That's true.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:59.701
Well, Scarlett did.
-Scarlett had the baby, yeah.

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:02.934
Have you met the baby?
-I have, man.

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.901
What a cute kid.
But babies are --

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:09.934
they're fun for, like, a second.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:13.667
You know, they don't do much
after you've looked at them.

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:16.534
And they're just staring at you,

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:17.934
trying to
keep their head on straight.

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:19.267
-Oh, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:21.133
-Get this wiggly thing
away from me.

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:23.200
But, no, it's, like,
an adorable baby.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.067
It's Colin and Scarlett's baby
together.

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:28.033
-Are you going to babysit?
Has he asked you yet?

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:29.400
-I don't like babysitting, man.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.334
I'm actually a really good
babysitter, though,

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:34.000
if you guys are interested.
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.234
I'm a great babysitter.

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:36.701
I've been babysitting
my whole life.

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:37.968
I have nieces and nephews

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:40.234
that's like
three years younger than me.

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:42.067
-Oh, really?
-I've been babysitting them

00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:45.067
since they were babies.
Since I was a baby, actually.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:48.434
-Yeah,
Were you a good babysitter?

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.834
-I was a great babysitter, man.

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:51.601
I just let you cry
until you're sleepy.

00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:53.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:57.100
-Now, "Michael Che:
Shame the Devil."

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.634
This is your stand-up special
on Netflix.

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:02.300
-I'm excited.
You know, right about now,

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.734
I just feel like
what the world needs is

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:07.534
more stand-up comedy on Netflix.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:10.200
Something that everyone
can agree on.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.367
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:14.467
I love the name
"Shame the Devil."

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:16.234
I've never heard that term
before.

00:03:16.234 --> 00:03:18.033
-Never? You don't got,
like, a black aunt?

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:20.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:23.534
"Shame the Devil" is a very --
it's something that, you know,

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:24.934
like, church ladies say.

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:26.334
They say, "Tell the truth,
shame the devil,

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:29.234
'cause the devil is a liar."
No one has ever heard this

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:31.400
before?
-No, I mean, I haven't.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.501
-The Roots are shaking their
head, "Yes, absolutely."

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.234
[ Laughter ]
"Shame the devil."

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:37.934
-So, you're just kind of
just telling the truth?

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:40.300
-I'm trying to.
But as much as I can, you know.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.434
-Yeah, you're a great comic,
man.

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:46.200
-Let's not...
-Where did you film it?

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.534
-In Oakland.
Oakland, California.

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:50.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.767
-A lot of Oakland fans here.
What's it like backstage

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:55.334
when you're on the road?
Do you have a rider?

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:56.901
Do you have --
What do you have in the room?

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:58.968
-I'm fascinated with riders.

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:00.367
Like, I don't really
have a rider.

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:02.300
I usually just ask for, like,
chicken fingers and M&amp;M's

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.834
because that's just
my life right now.

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:08.701
But I'm fascinated
with other people's riders.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:11.234
Like, I'm always like --
Anytime there's a performer,

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:13.067
like, before me, I'm like,
"What did they have

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:14.400
in their rider?"
And then, like, they tell me.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.200
Like, some performers --
one comedian --

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.267
I won't say his name,
but he asked for,

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:20.367
like, white sneakers
before every show.

00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:22.167
Brand-new white sneakers.
They got to buy them

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:24.834
before every show.
-Can you do that?

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:26.901
-Apparently, yeah.
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:26.901 --> 00:04:28.968
Isn't that the coolest thing?
You do it, too?

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.701
-i do it with T-shirts
and other things.

00:04:31.701 --> 00:04:33.501
But I like to provide
my own shoes.

00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:36.234
-That's awesome!
-Wait, do you go do a gig

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:38.634
and you have them buy you --
-I mean, you have a rider.

00:04:38.634 --> 00:04:41.968
It's, you know, part of
the terms of agreement.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:44.000
-No, I understand
what a rider is.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.767
-So you put the sneakers
on the rider,

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:48.567
and then, you know --'
-They got to do it.

00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:50.634
-Yeah, mission accomplished.
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:52.067
-One less thing
you got to think about.

00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:54.367
My favorite rider thing
was Snoop Dogg.

00:04:54.367 --> 00:04:56.334
I was doing a gig,

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:58.234
and Snoop Dogg was there,
like, the week before me.

00:04:58.234 --> 00:05:01.067
And it was in the U.K.,
and I was like,

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.667
"Man, what does Snoop Dogg have
in his rider?"

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:06.901
He said, "Regular stuff, but he
ordered 150 pounds of chicken."

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:09.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:12.133
And I was like,
"150 pounds of chicken?"

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:13.968
It blew my mind.
For, like, a whole year,

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:15.734
I'm thinking, "Snoop Dogg
eats more chicken

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:17.968
than anybody on the planet."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:20.000
And then I was telling a friend
about it.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.567
I was like, "You know Snoop Dogg
asks for 150 pounds of chicken

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:23.934
in the U.K.?"
And she was like,

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:27.934
"Money or weight?"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:31.267
-Oh. That makes more sense.
-Yeah, apparently,

00:05:31.267 --> 00:05:33.901
he doesn't eat a barrel of
chicken before shows.

00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:37.701
-Where does he put it all?
He's got good metabolism, man.

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:39.567
-It made the story
a lot less interesting.

00:05:39.567 --> 00:05:42.067
[ Laughter ]
-I want to show a clip.

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:44.067
If you guys needed a laugh,
you got to watch this.

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:46.567
Here's Michael Che
in "Shame the Devil" on Netflix.

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:47.734
Take a look.

00:05:47.734 --> 00:05:49.234
-Black people
love this country.

00:05:49.234 --> 00:05:51.801
We're just more specific
about our love.

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:53.801
You ask any [Bleep],
"You love America?"

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:56.334
he's like, "I love Brooklyn."

00:05:56.334 --> 00:05:58.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.501 --> 00:06:01.467
"Atlanta is cool.

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:03.634
I don't know [Bleep]
about them Dakotas."

00:06:03.634 --> 00:06:05.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.868
If there was
a black American flag,

00:06:06.868 --> 00:06:09.334
there'd be like 11 stars.

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:11.000
[ Laughter ]
For cities.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.234
It wouldn't even be
the whole state.

00:06:12.234 --> 00:06:15.300
They'd be like, "Alright,
Detroit, Oakland, D.C."

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:25.434
Everything else would be
a big-ass question mark.

00:06:25.434 --> 00:06:28.300
-That's what I'm talking about.
Michael Che, everybody!.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
His special "Shame the Devil"

00:06:30.634 --> 00:06:32.634
premieres on Netflix,
November 16th.

